SAY   SST-2 The Stanford Sentiment Treebank is a binary single-sentence classification task consisting of sentences extracted from movie reviews with human annotations of their sentiment (Socher and others, 2013).
PAUSE 500
SAY   CoLA The Corpus of Linguistic Acceptability is a binary single-sentence classification task, where the goal is to predict whether an English sentence is linguistically "acceptable" or not (Warstadt and others, 2018).
PAUSE 500
SAY   STS-B The Semantic Textual Similarity Benchmark is a collection of sentence pairs drawn from news headlines and other sources (Cer and others, 2017). They were annotated with a score from 1 to 5 denoting how similar the two sentences are in terms of semantic meaning.
PAUSE 500
SAY   MRPC Microsoft Research Paraphrase Corpus consists of sentence pairs automatically extracted from online news sources, with human annotations
PAUSE 500
SAY   for whether the sentences in the pair are semantically equivalent (Dolan and Brockett, 2005).
PAUSE 500
SAY   RTE Recognizing Textual Entailment is a binary entailment task similar to MNLI, but with much less training data (Bentivogli and others, 2009).14
PAUSE 500
SAY   WNLI Winograd NLI is a small natural language inference dataset (Levesque and others, 2011). The GLUE webpage notes that there are issues with the construction of this dataset, 15 and every trained system that's been submitted to GLUE has performed worse than the 65.1 baseline accuracy of predicting the majority class. We therefore exclude this set to be fair to OpenAI GPT. For our GLUE submission, we always predicted the ma-
