SAY   C Additional Ablation Studies
PAUSE 500
SAY   C.1 Effect of Number of Training Steps
PAUSE 500
SAY   1. Question: Does BERT really need such a large amount of pre-training (128,000 words/batch * 1,000,000 steps) to achieve high fine-tuning accuracy? Answer: Yes, BERTBASE achieves almost 1.0 percent additional accuracy on MNLI when trained on 1M steps compared to 500k steps.
PAUSE 500
SAY   2. Question: Does MLM pre-training converge slower than LTR pre-training, since only 15 percent of words are predicted in each batch rather than every word? Answer: The MLM model does converge slightly slower than the LTR model. However, in terms of absolute accuracy the MLM model begins to outperform the LTR model almost immediately.
PAUSE 500
SAY   C.2 Ablation for Different Masking Procedures
PAUSE 500
SAY   In Section 3.1, we mention that BERT uses a mixed strategy for masking the target tokens when pre-training with the masked language model (MLM) objective. The following is an ablation study to evaluate the effect of different masking strategies.
PAUSE 500
SAY   BERTBASE (Masked LM) BERTBASE (Left-to-Right)
PAUSE 500
SAY   200 400 600 800 1,000
PAUSE 500
SAY   Pre-training Steps (Thousands)
PAUSE 500
SAY   Note that the purpose of the masking strategies is to reduce the mismatch between pre-training and fine-tuning, as the [MASK] symbol never appears during the fine-tuning stage. We report the Dev results for both MNLI and NER. For NER, we report both fine-tuning and feature-based approaches, as we expect the mismatch will be amplified for the feature-based approach as the model will not have the chance to adjust the representations.
